{
 "schema_version": 1,
 "description": "Construction-adjacency memory on writerslogic-02 (WSL2, Intel Core Ultra 9 185H, x86_64 Linux), SIFT-1M (sift-128-euclidean, 1,000,000 rows, 10,000 test queries), public-bench ann-qgraph --index vertex, 10 rayon threads, two runs per binary, interleaved by run (bc03737, 175a292, cf7f7c6, then again). peak_rss is the whole process maximum resident set from /usr/bin/time -v; rss_after_build and build_secs come from the public-bench record. QPS is single-threaded on a shared host and is recorded but not compared; the claim is build time, memory, an unchanged graph hash and identical recall at every sweep point.",
 "command": "public-bench ann-qgraph --data data/sift-128-euclidean --out <run>.json --metric euclidean --index vertex --degree 64 --build-ef 500 --quantized-search --vertex-bits 8 --residual --residual-bits 8 --align-rows --reorder --id-bytes 3 --rerank 32,64 --repeats 1 --max-wait-secs 0",
 "command_wrapper": "each run held the host timing lock (flock) and ran as taskset -c 12-21 /usr/bin/time -v <command>; the 10 pinned CPUs give rayon 10 threads",
